On my first run, I ran out of GD scrolls on the plane of water but
fortunately I had some magic marker charges remaining.  I'd recommend
that you keep some spare charges and some blank scrolls for the run.
Do you have any spare destroy armor scrolls?  If so, use those for
fooproofing instead of EA.

> 3. Create stack of 200+ blessed rustproof +7 arrows with Longbow
> of Diana and magic markers. (laughs manically) Extra weapon
> scrolls go to Magicbane.

Fighting time is basically over.  If you haven't used up the markers,
save them.  Once you kill the Wizard, grab the book and run.  Once you
kill the priest, grab the amulet and run.  With the notable exception
of the Riders and the Wizard, the monsters aren't going to be getting
any harder at this point, instead what happens is that you are mobbed,
in which case better AC helps or a broken wand of teleport (x:1) is a
great move.  Kill Rodney, Pestilence or Famine with a wand of death;
kill Death with Melee.  Overall, you're better off with scrolls of
charging and wands of death and teleport than better weapons, IMHO.
>
> 4. Last Wishes in order of priority:
> = of Conflict.

This is a great ring.  The other ring I like is teleport control if
you don't have the intrinsic.  It makes the ascension run very very
fast, if you know where the upstairs are, and if you have spare
teleport scrolls.  Another nice wish, magic marker use, or divine gift
would be a spellbook of magic mapping.  It looks like a ranger with
Int=17, wearing a robe, with skilled divination can cast MM at 0%
failure.

> +2 =of Increase Damage

As someone else already mentioned, a well-timed rubber chicken will
serve you better.

